Hello,

I have this main Rnw file:
\documentclass{article}
\begin{document}

%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
\section{Using knit\_expand}

<<>>=
out <- NULL
for(value in 1:2){
    out <- c(out, knit_expand("child.Rnw"))
}
@

\Sexpr{paste(knit(text = out), collapse = '\n')}

%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
\section{Using knit\_child}

<<>>=
out <- NULL
for(value in 1:2){
    out <- c(out, knit_child("child.Rnw", quiet=TRUE))
}
@

\Sexpr{paste(knit(text = out), collapse = '\n')}

\end{document}

And child.Rnw:
\texttt{\{\{value\}\}} is {{value}}.

\medskip

\texttt{value} is \Sexpr{value}.

\bigskip

This is the output when I knit the main Rnw:

 <https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-8omeEferU-M/WG0FWnOtKcI/AAAAAAAAAHU/ra-2ocqXYpMWU3VYfCW37jePVe97lwplwCLcB/s1600/Capture.PNG>

I don't understand why "value" is always "2" with knit_expand. Can someone explain that ? Thanks.

